{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "what_this_is": "SetAsidePolicy, measured. The question is whether sizing the L2 set-aside from the workload beats the constant fraction every prior number in this repository was measured under. At batch 1 it does, resolved and replicated across three runs and two rebuilds. At four concurrent sequences the axis does not resolve, and the one run that did resolve did not replicate -- that run is kept here because half the design was built on it. NOT SCORABLE: this checkpoint is not reproducible against itself (see results/rtx5090-moe-scored.json and the changelog's checkpoint survey), so these are throughput numbers and evidence for a planner rule, and decide.py refuses them, correctly.",
