  "concurrency4": {
    "workload": "concurrency 4 aggregate, 3 interleaved pairs, 1 warm-up discarded",
    "verdict": "OPEN. Two of three runs do not resolve. Runs 1 and 3 held the SAME 60 MiB reservation and measured -0.99% and -0.28%, so the between-run spread on one configuration is about 0.7 points against per-run floors of 0.13-0.41%: this arm is not reproducible across rebuilds on this checkpoint. The -0.99% is one unreplicated observation and must not be quoted as the cost of the policy.",
    "residency_excluded": "At four sequences the resident fraction is 0.478, below the 0.50 threshold, so Residency declines the reservation outright and real_eval.py's null-candidate guard refuses the arm BY NAME. That is correct -- a policy whose response to pressure is to install nothing IS baseline -- so its value here is baseline by construction, and the refusal is the observation that it declined.",
